		<ParagraphStyleRange AppliedParagraphStyle="ParagraphStyle/A4 V%3aSubhead Large">
			<CharacterStyleRange AppliedCharacterStyle="CharacterStyle/$ID/[No character style]">
				<Content>Trackwork Rider Program</Content>
				<Br />
			</CharacterStyleRange>
		</ParagraphStyleRange>
		<ParagraphStyleRange AppliedParagraphStyle="ParagraphStyle/A4 V%3aBody">
			<CharacterStyleRange AppliedCharacterStyle="CharacterStyle/$ID/[No character style]">
				<Content>Launched in 2023, the Trackwork Rider Program — delivered in partnership with the Racing Education Centre — is the only program of its kind in Australia to provide structured, off-the-job training for aspiring trackwork riders.</Content>
				<Br />
				<Content>Since its inception, more than 50 riders have 
enrolled in the program, with many progressing to stable employment or advancing to further professional development through the Rider Development Squad (RDS).</Content>
				<Br />
				<Content>The appointment of ex-jockey Nathan Rose as the program’s dedicated coach has further strengthened delivery, providing consistent, individualised support to participants and contributing to the program’s continued growth and success.</Content>
				<Br />
			</CharacterStyleRange>
		</ParagraphStyleRange>
		<ParagraphStyleRange AppliedParagraphStyle="ParagraphStyle/A4 V%3aSubhead Large">
			<CharacterStyleRange AppliedCharacterStyle="CharacterStyle/$ID/[No character style]">
				<Content>Rider Development Squad</Content>
				<Br />
			</CharacterStyleRange>
		</ParagraphStyleRange>
		<ParagraphStyleRange AppliedParagraphStyle="ParagraphStyle/A4 V%3aBody">
			<CharacterStyleRange AppliedCharacterStyle="CharacterStyle/$ID/[No character style]">
				<Content>The RDS builds upon the foundational skills of emerging trackwork riders, preparing them for potential selection for the Apprentice Jockey Training Program (AJTP) and/or assisting them in improving their trackwork riding skills and overall health.</Content>
				<Br />
			</CharacterStyleRange>
		</ParagraphStyleRange>
		<ParagraphStyleRange AppliedParagraphStyle="ParagraphStyle/A4 V%3aBody" SpaceAfter="8.78740157480315">
			<CharacterStyleRange AppliedCharacterStyle="CharacterStyle/$ID/[No character style]">
				<Content>In FY25, 70 participants took part in the program, attending sessions at RV’s headquarters which included:</Content>
				<Br />
			</CharacterStyleRange>
		</ParagraphStyleRange>
		<ParagraphStyleRange AppliedParagraphStyle="ParagraphStyle/B3 Bullets" LeftIndent="22.67716535433071" FirstLineIndent="-22.67716535433071" SpaceAfter="8.78740157480315" GridAlignment="None">
			<CharacterStyleRange AppliedCharacterStyle="CharacterStyle/$ID/[No character style]">
				<Content>Strength, conditioning and recovery sessions with the Victorian Institute of Sport (VIS);</Content>
				<Br />
				<Content>Mechanical horse training, nutrition and wellbeing education; and</Content>
				<Br />
			</CharacterStyleRange>
		</ParagraphStyleRange>
		<ParagraphStyleRange AppliedParagraphStyle="ParagraphStyle/B3 Bullets" LeftIndent="22.67716535433071" FirstLineIndent="-22.67716535433071" GridAlignment="None">
			<CharacterStyleRange AppliedCharacterStyle="CharacterStyle/$ID/[No character style]">
				<Content>Access to RV’s multidisciplinary support team (jockey coaches, mentors, physiotherapists, dietitians and sports psychologists).</Content>
				<Br />
			</CharacterStyleRange>
		</ParagraphStyleRange>
		<ParagraphStyleRange AppliedParagraphStyle="ParagraphStyle/A4 V%3aSubhead Large">
			<CharacterStyleRange AppliedCharacterStyle="CharacterStyle/$ID/[No character style]">
				<Content>Pony Club Victoria Ride 
to Time Partnership</Content>
				<Br />
			</CharacterStyleRange>
		</ParagraphStyleRange>
		<ParagraphStyleRange AppliedParagraphStyle="ParagraphStyle/A4 V%3aBody">
			<CharacterStyleRange AppliedCharacterStyle="CharacterStyle/$ID/[No character style]">
				<Content>In FY25, RV re-established its partnership with Pony Club Victoria (PCV) to deliver the Ride to Time program — an initiative designed to introduce young riders to pace awareness, control, and riding safety 
in a structured and educational environment.</Content>
				<Br />
				<Content>Throughout the year, RV’s Workforce Development Team and professional jockey Tayla Childs supported the PCV Zone Series, attending each zone at least once during their qualifier rounds. Beyond the competition series, RV also provided hands-on coaching to 25 Pony Clubs across Victoria, delivering Ride to Time sessions at local rally days.</Content>
				<Br />
				<Content>The Ride to Time Series Final, held at Moonee Valley Racecourse in September, comprised a finalist from each zone and provided participants and their families with a memorable raceday experience. This renewed partnership has created an exciting and effective grassroots connection between the equestrian and racing communities.</Content>
				<Br />
			</CharacterStyleRange>
		</ParagraphStyleRange>
		<ParagraphStyleRange AppliedParagraphStyle="ParagraphStyle/A4 V%3aSubhead Large">
			<CharacterStyleRange AppliedCharacterStyle="CharacterStyle/$ID/[No character style]">
				<Content>Apprentice Jockey Training Program</Content>
				<Br />
			</CharacterStyleRange>
		</ParagraphStyleRange>
		<ParagraphStyleRange AppliedParagraphStyle="ParagraphStyle/A4 V%3aBody">
			<CharacterStyleRange AppliedCharacterStyle="CharacterStyle/$ID/[No character style]">
				<Content>The AJTP continues to be recognised nationally as the leading development pathway for emerging jockeys.</Content>
				<Br />
				<Content>In FY25, RV introduced a new initiative — 
the Apprentice Jockey Squad (AJS) — to create 
a pathway from the RDS to the full AJTP. The AJS allows RV to work with a larger group of potential apprentices and ensures participants can be assessed and supported over time, without the pressure of entering into a formal contract.</Content>
				<Br />
				<Content>The inaugural AJS intake included 12 riders (pictured), with 10 remaining active in the program as of June 2025. This approach has strengthened the overall pathway from grassroots participation to professional licensing, ensuring that those who progress into the AJTP are well-prepared and committed.</Content>
				<Br />
				<Br />
				<Content>Across the year, there were 40 apprentices undertaking training within the AJTP, spanning Years 1–4, and another seven graduate apprentice jockeys. </Content>
				<Br />
				<Content>At the 2025 Apprentice Graduation and Awards Night, the following achievements were recognised:</Content>
				<Br />
			</CharacterStyleRange>
